From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mpl: settle missing tilings with the exact check (MPL-0003)

MPL-0003 said only that annealing found no tiling. When no run finds
one, the exact check now either finds an arrangement, whose bounding box
becomes the tiling, or proves that none exists, and the error says why
and which single change to the core fixes it, on the row and site grid:

  [ERROR MPL-0003] There are no valid tilings for mixed cluster root.
  The blocks, halos included, cannot fit in the 108.432 x 108.270 um
  outline (proven).
    Cause: the area suffices (83% of the outline), but no arrangement of
    the blocks does.
    It fits with any one of:
      same width 108.432 um: height >= 109.350 um
      same height 108.270 um: width >= 109.350 um
      same aspect ratio: width >= 109.296 um
    The outline is the core area.

That is asap7/aes-block at a core of 110.5 um; a core 109.350 um wide
(2025 sites) places, one site narrower does not. A problem the check
cannot decide within its budget keeps the plain error; the README's
limitations say so.

Not upstreamed; retires at the //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.

---
diff --git a/src/mpl/README.md b/src/mpl/README.md
index 08d6d00347..e847eeb6d4 100644
--- a/src/mpl/README.md
+++ b/src/mpl/README.md
@@ -174,6 +174,12 @@ bazelisk test //src/mpl/...
 
 ## Limitations
 
+- When annealing finds no tiling or no placement for a cluster, an exact
+  check (OR-tools CP-SAT) settles whether one exists, on a deterministic
+  budget. A problem it cannot decide within that budget gets the error
+  without a proof; this happens when the macros fill nearly all of the
+  outline (on the ORFS designs, one problem at 99% fill).
+
 ## References
 1. A. B. Kahng, R. Varadarajan and Z. Wang, 
 "RTL-MP: Toward Practical, Human-Quality Chip Planning and Macro Placement",
diff --git a/src/mpl/src/hier_rtlmp.cpp b/src/mpl/src/hier_rtlmp.cpp
index 34ca4b2386..8283a1a8b5 100644
--- a/src/mpl/src/hier_rtlmp.cpp
+++ b/src/mpl/src/hier_rtlmp.cpp
@@ -410,6 +410,23 @@ void HierRTLMP::setRootShapes()
 // Ignore all the standard-cell clusters.
 // At this stage, we assume the standard cell placer will automatically
 // place standard cells in the empty space between macros.
+std::string HierRTLMP::explainOutline(const PackingProblem& problem,
+                                      const PackingResult& result) const
+{
+  // Outlines snap to sites and rows, so the fixes are on that grid.
+  int site_width = 1;
+  int row_height = 1;
+  for (odb::dbRow* row : block_->getRows()) {
+    site_width = row->getSite()->getWidth();
+    row_height = row->getSite()->getHeight();
+    break;
+  }
+  return explainDoesNotFit(problem,
+                           result,
+                           findFixes(problem, site_width, row_height),
+                           block_->getDbUnitsPerMicron());
+}
+
 void HierRTLMP::warnIfTight(const PackingProblem& problem) const
 {
   // Measuring the room costs exact checks; only near-full cores pay it.
@@ -687,10 +704,37 @@ void HierRTLMP::calculateChildrenTilings(Cluster* parent)
   }
 
   if (tilings_set.empty()) {
-    logger_->error(MPL,
-                   3,
-                   "There are no valid tilings for mixed cluster: {}",
-                   parent->getName());
+    // No annealing run found an arrangement; settle whether one exists.
+    const PackingProblem problem = toPackingProblem(outline, macros, 0);
+    const PackingResult fit = checkPacking(problem);
+    if (fit.status == PackingStatus::kFits) {
+      int width = 0;
+      int height = 0;
+      for (const PlacedBlock& block : fit.placement) {
+        width = std::max(width, block.x + block.width);
+        height = std::max(height, block.y + block.height);
+      }
+      debugPrint(logger_,
+                 MPL,
+                 "coarse_shaping",
+                 1,
+                 "Annealing found no tiling for {}; the exact check found "
+                 "{} x {}",
+                 parent->getName(),
+                 width,
+                 height);
+      tilings_set.insert({width, height});
+    } else {
+      logger_->error(
+          MPL,
+          3,
+          "There are no valid tilings for mixed cluster {}{}",
+          parent->getName(),
+          fit.status == PackingStatus::kDoesNotFit
+              ? ". " + explainOutline(problem, fit)
+                    + "\n  The outline is the core area."
+              : "; the exact check could not decide within its budget.");
+    }
   }
 
   if (parent == tree_->root.get()) {
diff --git a/src/mpl/src/hier_rtlmp.h b/src/mpl/src/hier_rtlmp.h
index 7986a6b6d4..e5e0db63b5 100644
--- a/src/mpl/src/hier_rtlmp.h
+++ b/src/mpl/src/hier_rtlmp.h
@@ -148,6 +148,9 @@ class HierRTLMP
   void runCoarseShaping();
   void setRootShapes();
   void calculateChildrenTilings(Cluster* parent);
+  // Why `problem` does not fit, with the outline changes that would fix it.
+  std::string explainOutline(const PackingProblem& problem,
+                             const PackingResult& result) const;
   // Warn when the core leaves the macros next to no room.
   void warnIfTight(const PackingProblem& problem) const;
   void calculateMacroTilings(Cluster* cluster);
